{% doc %}
Emits shippingDetails and hasMerchantReturnPolicy for an Offer node.

Every value here is transcribed from a source NUR actually publishes — the
delivery profiles configured in Shopify, /pages/shipping-policy, and
/pages/widerrufsrecht. Nothing is estimated. If a rate or a window changes in
Shopify or on those pages, change it here too; do not let the two drift.

Starts with a comma and is rendered immediately after the Offer's "seller"
object, so the caller needs no separator of its own.
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Zones exactly as configured in the "General profile" delivery profile.
  endcomment
  assign nur_eu_zone = 'AT,BE,BG,HR,CY,CZ,DK,EE,FI,FR,GR,HU,IE,IT,LV,LT,LU,MT,NL,PL,PT,RO,SK,SI,ES,SE' | split: ','
  assign nur_intl_zone = 'AE,AU,CA,CH,GB,HK,IL,JP,KR,MY,NO,NZ,SG,US' | split: ','
  assign nur_return_countries = 'DE,AT,BE,BG,HR,CY,CZ,DK,EE,FI,FR,GR,HU,IE,IT,LV,LT,LU,MT,NL,PL,PT,RO,SK,SI,ES,SE' | split: ','
-%}
,"shippingDetails": [
  {%- comment -%}
    Germany. 5.99 is the standard rate; free shipping above a threshold is a
    promotion disclosed on the linked policy page rather than a second rate here,
    because schema.org has no clean way to express "free over X" and quoting the
    free rate as the default would understate what most customers pay.
    Transit uses the EU standard window from the policy, since the policy states
    no separate domestic figure and inventing a faster one is not an option.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {
    "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
    "shippingRate": {"@type": "MonetaryAmount", "value": 5.99, "currency": "EUR"},
    "shippingDestination": {"@type": "DefinedRegion", "addressCountry": "DE"},
    "deliveryTime": {
      "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
      "handlingTime": {"@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 1, "maxValue": 3, "unitCode": "DAY"},
      "transitTime": {"@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 3, "maxValue": 7, "unitCode": "DAY"}
    },
    "shippingSettingsLink": {{ shop.url | append: '/pages/shipping-policy' | json }}
  },
  {
    "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
    "shippingRate": {"@type": "MonetaryAmount", "value": 5.90, "currency": "EUR"},
    "shippingDestination": {"@type": "DefinedRegion", "addressCountry": [
      {%- for c in nur_eu_zone -%}{{ c | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}
    ]},
    "deliveryTime": {
      "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
      "handlingTime": {"@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 1, "maxValue": 3, "unitCode": "DAY"},
      "transitTime": {"@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 3, "maxValue": 7, "unitCode": "DAY"}
    },
    "shippingSettingsLink": {{ shop.url | append: '/pages/shipping-policy' | json }}
  },
  {
    "@type": "OfferShippingDetails",
    "shippingRate": {"@type": "MonetaryAmount", "value": 19.99, "currency": "EUR"},
    "shippingDestination": {"@type": "DefinedRegion", "addressCountry": [
      {%- for c in nur_intl_zone -%}{{ c | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}
    ]},
    "deliveryTime": {
      "@type": "ShippingDeliveryTime",
      "handlingTime": {"@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 1, "maxValue": 3, "unitCode": "DAY"},
      "transitTime": {"@type": "QuantitativeValue", "minValue": 7, "maxValue": 14, "unitCode": "DAY"}
    },
    "shippingSettingsLink": {{ shop.url | append: '/pages/shipping-policy' | json }}
  }
],
{%- comment -%}
  IMPORTANT - read before editing this block.

  The 14-day window is the statutory Widerrufsrecht under section 312g BGB, and
  it is quoted verbatim from /pages/widerrufsrecht ("binnen vierzehn Tagen").

  That page ALSO excludes opened fragrances: under section 312g Abs. 2 Nr. 3 BGB
  the right lapses for sealed goods once the seal is broken, so only UNOPENED,
  sealed decants and gift sets are returnable. schema.org has no field for that
  condition, which is why merchantReturnLink is mandatory here rather than
  optional - it is the only thing disclosing the exclusion. Never remove it, and
  never "simplify" this block into a bare 14-day claim.

  returnFees is ReturnFeesCustomerResponsibility because the page states "Sie
  tragen die unmittelbaren Kosten der Rucksendung der Waren". That enumeration
  needs no amount, which is correct - NUR charges no return fee, the customer
  arranges and pays their own carrier.

  applicableCountry is DE plus the EU zone only. The statutory right follows EU
  consumer law, so asserting it for the international zone would be wrong.
{%- endcomment -%}
"hasMerchantReturnPolicy": {
  "@type": "MerchantReturnPolicy",
  "applicableCountry": [
    {%- for c in nur_return_countries -%}{{ c | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}{%- endfor -%}
  ],
  "returnPolicyCategory": "https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow",
  "merchantReturnDays": 14,
  "returnMethod": "https://schema.org/ReturnByMail",
  "returnFees": "https://schema.org/ReturnFeesCustomerResponsibility",
  "merchantReturnLink": {{ shop.url | append: '/pages/widerrufsrecht' | json }}
}
